   "evidence": "A grep for `ofHom_mem_dgCycles` and for `ofHom.*\u2208.*dgCycles` in TauCeti finds nothing. The same fact is also proved inline at CochainComplex/HomotopyCategory.lean:80 (`(mem_dgCycles R).2 ((dgDifferential_linearHomComplex R 0 _).trans (\u03b4_ofHom f))`).",
   "file": "TauCeti/CategoryTheory/DG/CochainComplex/KInjective.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public `KInjectiveDGCategory.ofHom_mem_dgCycles (f : K \u27f6 L) : Cochain.ofHom f \u2208 dgCycles R \u27e8K,_\u27e9 \u27e8L,_\u27e9` and use `hf := ofHom_mem_dgCycles R C f` as the default in both theorems.",
   "issue": "The `hf` default (closedness of `Cochain.ofHom f` in `dgCycles`) is the same three-line tactic script pasted into both `isEquivalence_edgeMk_iff_quasiIso` (l.201) and `isEquivalence_edgeMk_iff_isIso_homologyMap` (l.220). The fact always holds, but no public lemma states it, so anyone building the edge of a chain map (e.g. for `toDerivedCategory_map_homOf`, l.121) has to re-derive it.",
